    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="1178" n="1131" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg1131"/>

                <head>693. Telegram 135 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d693-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1956-08-08">August 8, 1956</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d693-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d693-1"/>
                <p>135. For Johnson.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You will note clear implication in Department’s press release (Deptel 134)
                        that Americans would be allowed travel Communist China once all America
                        prisoners released. Without making this implication explicit, you should
                        exploit it in August 9 meeting so that meaning will be clear to Communists
                        and maximum leverage will be exerted on them to release Americans.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>FYI American Red Cross has agreed to interview Chinese prisoners in US.
                        Communists should not be informed of this at meeting.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d693-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d693-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/8–856. Confidential; Niact;
                    Limit Distribution. Drafted by Clough; cleared by Phleger and McConaughy and in
                    substance by Sebald. The time of transmission is illegible.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
